{"metadata":{"externalID":"s:6Cycles017DirectedChordlessA0V","modules":[{"name":"Cycles"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","title":"DirectedChordlessCycles","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedChordlessCycles"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Cycles\/ChordlessCycles.swift#L273","fileName":"ChordlessCycles.swift"},"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedChordlessCycles","kind":"identifier"}]},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedChordlessCycles","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A self-loop is a chordless cycle when it is its vertex’s only one, and its vertex is on no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other; two opposite edges are one when nothing else joins their ends. A parallel edge is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"chord of every cycle through its ends."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The sequence holds the graph (a value), so iterating again gives the same cycles. The first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next()"},{"type":"text","text":" copies the graph’s rows, O(n + m). The search extends only induced paths, each step"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(d) for the degree d of the vertex entered or left."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/cycles\/directedchordlesscycles"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles\/DirectedChordlessCycles","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Cycles\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Cycles\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/Cycles\/ST"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Every chordless cycle of a directed graph once, lazily: the simple cycles whose vertices","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"induce no edge but the cycle’s own. By least vertex (in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order), and among the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cycles with one least vertex in the order a depth-first search from it, taking out-edges in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges"},{"text":" order, meets them.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles\/DirectedChordlessCycles\/Iterator"],"anchor":"Structures","generated":true},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles\/DirectedChordlessCycles\/maxLength"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true},{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles\/DirectedChordlessCycles\/makeIterator()"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true},{"title":"Type Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles\/DirectedChordlessCycles\/Element"],"anchor":"Type-Aliases","generated":true},{"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles\/